  "id": "COMPOUND:19085 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that SureCN26387 interacts with SNU-387 through a series of target relationships, all centered on hepatocytes and other compounds. The core mechanism appears to involve the hepatocyte as a common target, with multiple compounds—such as 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, and Licochalcone D—acting as intermediaries in the interaction with SNU-387. These compounds are all known to target SNU-387, indicating a potential pathway where SureCN26387 may influence SNU-387 through these intermediates. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where SureCN26387 is linked to hepatocytes, which in turn are linked to SNU-387 via multiple compounds. This suggests a possible mechanism involving the hepatocyte as a central node in the interaction network, with SureCN26387 acting as a modulator or regulator of the pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction, emphasizing the role of hepatocytes and their associated compounds in linking SureCN26387 to SNU-387.",
